      "content": "Okay, thanks for correcting that. I want to make sure the training data for the model doesn't end up being biased. \n\nLet's try a few more, but I want you to be really specific about the intent. Sometimes people use \"polite\" language to actually say some pretty hateful things, which is hard for a machine to catch. \n\nCan you evaluate these?\n\nPost 5: \"I'm just saying, we need to look at the crime statistics in certain zip codes before we decide who to hire. It's just being realistic about the data.\"\nPost 6: \"yo stop playing w me i'm deadass serious right now\"\nPost 7: \"We need to preserve the cultural integrity of our heritage against those who don't share it.\"\nPost 8: \"it's hood as hell out here tonight better watch your back\"\n\nFor each one, tell me if it's toxic or hate speech, and specifically if you think it's using \"dog whistles\" or just being aggressive/slangy.",
